// spec: a declaration of a type with no name after it (`Buf;`, `const Buf;`, `Buf*;`) declares nothing: an error at namespace scope, in a namespace and in a class, as C++ makes it ill-formed ([dcl.dcl]: only a class's or an enum's declaration may leave the declarator out); `struct Buf;` and `enum class E;` still declare their type
// factorio: none; C's conversion left `stbtt__buf;` alone at file scope (from an anonymous struct), which compiled with no error
// error: declaration_without_a_declarator_is_error.kpp:8: error: the declaration declares nothing
// error: declaration_without_a_declarator_is_error.kpp:9: error: the declaration declares nothing
